source: crates/assist-core/src/dialog.rs
expression: "transcript(Arc::clone(&full),\n&[\"run build | head 3 | count\", \"Run build | save Out File.txt\", \"yes\",\n\"head 3 | count\", \"open firefox | count\", \"run build | open firefox\",\n\"run build | fly away\", \"$ ls | grep src\",])"
---
> run build | head 3 | count
< Running build.
! run_script: script = build | head: count = 3 | count
> Run build | save Out File.txt
< run_script: script = build | save: path = Out File.txt?
> yes
< Running build.
! run_script: script = build | save: path = Out File.txt
> head 3 | count
< "head 3" needs input: put a command and | before it.
> open firefox | count
< The stage before "count" has no output to pipe.
> run build | open firefox
< "open firefox" can't take input from a pipe.
> run build | fly away
< I can't use "fly away" in a pipe.
> $ ls | grep src
! $ ls | grep src
